23:["$","$L3c",null,{"faqs":[{"question":"What is nearshore software development?","answer":"Nearshore software development is hiring a software team in a nearby country in your time zone — for US companies, typically Mexico — instead of offshore (a far country with a large time-zone gap) or building in-house. You get senior talent, real-time collaboration, and lower cost than US hiring."},{"question":"Why nearshore to Mexico instead of offshore to India?","answer":"Speed of iteration. From Monterrey we work in your time zone with same-day feedback loops, 140 miles from the US border. Offshore's 12-hour gap means every question costs a day. For modern, fast-moving development, the overlapping hours matter more than the lowest hourly rate."},{"question":"How much does nearshore software development cost?","answer":"Rates sit between offshore and US in-house — typically a fraction of US salaries while delivering senior, US-aligned talent. We scope a fixed-price discovery first so you see the team, the plan, and the cost before committing to a build."},{"question":"Do we own the team and the code?","answer":"Yes. The engineers work as part of your team, you own all the code and IP, and you interview and approve every person. Part of every engagement is making the relationship transparent — no black-box resources."},{"question":"How fast can a nearshore team start?","answer":"Senior engineers can be embedded in days, not the months a US hire takes. We pre-vet talent matched to your stack, you interview, and the team plugs into your tools and rituals from week one."},{"question":"What nearshore software development services do you offer?","answer":"We offer three nearshore software development services: staff augmentation (senior engineers embedded into your existing team), dedicated teams (a full cross-functional pod run end-to-end from Monterrey), and full project builds (custom software from discovery to launch). Every model works in your time zone, ships with AI tooling baked in, and lets you interview and approve each engineer."},{"question":"How do I choose a nearshore software development company?","answer":"Look for a nearshore software development company in your time zone, with senior engineers you interview yourself, transparent pricing, and clear IP ownership. WeEvolveIT works from Monterrey in full US time-zone overlap, with 15+ years and 1,000+ projects delivered; you interview every engineer, own all the code and IP, and see a fixed-price scope before you commit."},{"question":"Why is Mexico the top destination for nearshore software development?","answer":"Mexico shares US time zones and sits 140 miles from the border at Monterrey, its industrial and tech capital, with a deep pool of senior engineers at a fraction of US rates. You get same-day, real-time collaboration, a short flight instead of a 24-hour journey, and strong US cultural alignment. That combination is why nearshore software development in Mexico is growing fast among US companies."}],"id":"faq","title":"What teams ask before going nearshore.","fill":true}]
